      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{2{x}^{2}+y}{{y}^{3}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\frac{2{x}^{2}+y}{{y}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}+y) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}(4x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
